    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d668">

                <pb facs="0648" n="1382" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1382"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic">December 6,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I made application to the Sultan for <hi rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi> to
                    visit Constantinople in order that I might have a consultation with admiral,
                    because the admiral requested me to do so. I know nothing of his instructions;
                    supposed he was authorized. Our war vessels have come here since the <pb
                        facs="0649" n="1383" xml:id="pg1383"/> treaty which closed Dardanelles. I
                    had reason to believe that the <hi rendition="#italic">Marblehead’s</hi> coming
                    would not be objected to by the treaty Powers. Massacre Cæsarea. Americans
                    safe.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
